#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:13
#: 2e7f816335c3496aa3c9aa88e9ae1da4
msgid "Remote IDs are becoming a legal requirement in some countries. Below is a list of devices compatible with ArduPilot. There is a quite nice explanation and list of frequently asked questions regarding Remote ID available `here <https://drone-remote-id.com/>`__ (site hosted by Dronetag)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:16
#: 282478fb4ad74d60b6b0299a1d332786
msgid "Variations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:18
#: fc05739fce964d57b3d6d7c95a03c795
msgid "There are basically two differing Remote ID requirements, although specifics vary according to country/region: devices integrated into OEM supplied systems, and add-on beacons for DIY and existing vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-remoteid.rst:20
#: c4c006b867844bf394e70077c3413812
msgid "For the ones users will be adding, there are variations on whether the device gets GPS position information via an integrated GPS or from the autopilot using its position and other information for its GPS. If connected to the autopilot for position and other information via MAVLink, either proprietary firmware or firmware conforming to the OpenDroneID standard is used to implement Remote ID(see following section) can be used. Power can be supplied either from the vehicle (MAVLink connection or to the vehicle's power), or via a small rechargeable battery (completely self contained units which can be transferred between vehicles easily)."
msgstr ""

